WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.868
-Hello, everyone.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.002
Welcome to "The Tonight Show
At Home Edition."

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.138
My name is Jimmy Fallon.
It is May 1st today.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.975
Actually wearing this
in honor of Gigi Bryant.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:10.743
Today would've been
her birthday

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.913
and so I'm going to do
the show in honor of Gigi

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.848
and play like Gigi,

00:00:15.848 --> 00:00:19.819
which is with all heart
and leading with kindness.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.655
I'm thinking about the whole
family today, guys.

00:00:22.655 --> 00:00:23.723
Let's get to some jokes.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.191
Here we go.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.759
Let's get to some news.
Governor Cuomo said that,

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.628
for the first time in history
the New York City subways

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:32.632
won't run 24/7, so that they
can be cleaned each night.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.134
Yeah, that's right.
It's better than the old way

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.301
they cleaned the subways --

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:38.604
taping a Swiffer pad to a rat.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.306
Some entertainment news.
I saw that Disney

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:43.942
is working on a live action
remake of "Hercules."

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:47.881
No word yet on who they want
to play Hercules, so...

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:52.318
just gonna put that out there
and...

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.586
wait for the call.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:59.926
An-y minute.

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:02.128
Disney will call.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.496
Just sayin'.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.664
Hercules.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.669
Hey, I wanna say congratulations
to Anderson Cooper,

00:01:10.669 --> 00:01:12.772
who's the father
of a new baby boy!

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.074
[ Clapping ]
Yay!

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.075
That's awesome.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:17.343
You can tell having a newborn

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.811
has already taken
its toll on him.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.646
Here is a photo
of Anderson on Monday

00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:23.749
and here he is today.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:25.151
I read that,
since the quarantine began,

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:28.021
"Jeopardy!" has had
very strong ratings.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.922
Well, I think it's starting
to affect the show.

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:32.525
Take a look at some of the
categories from last night.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:36.563
First, there's Name of Friends
You Forgot Existed.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:40.933
Next, there's Coworkers' Homes
You've Judged through Zoom.

00:01:40.933 --> 00:01:43.669
Then there's
"Sitting and Staring."

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:47.907
There's also
"Cocktails That Taste Bad,
But Get the Job Done."

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:51.510
And, finally, there's
Potent Edibles.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.212
Some sports news.
I saw this year's

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:56.148
Little League World Series
has been canceled.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.417
All the players heard that
and were like,

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:58.917
[ Baritone ] That sucks!
[ Inhales ]

00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:01.320
Well, back to quarantine.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.755
What's that?
When was I born?

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.756
Uh...

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.959
two thousand, uh...

00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:07.427
2014.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.698
Meanwhile, NASCAR announced
that it plans

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:14.601
to resume its season
on May 17th,

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.103
with seven races in 11 days.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.671
That's great.
What better way to spice up

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.005
living the same day
over and over

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:23.743
than watching guys driving
in a circle over and over?

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.711
This is cool --
LeBron James just unveiled

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:28.214
the title of next year's
"Space Jam" sequel.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:31.016
It's called
"Space Jam: A New Legacy."

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:32.752
Everyone's excited 'cause,
at this point,

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.053
50 million people would watch

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:36.256
Bugs Bunny take free throws
[ Laughing ] on ESPN.

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:43.128
Still waiting for that call
from the Disney folk.

00:02:43.128 --> 00:02:44.430
I read that,
because of the coronavirus,

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.267
actors may stop doing
sex scenes in movies.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.736
This is weird --
Once the news broke,

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.437
the running time
for "Space Jam 2"

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.905
was cut in half.

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.540
Wow!

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.708
And, finally,
I saw that Pillsbury

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.010
is now selling Funfetti cereal.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.979
Take a look this.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.347
Yeah. It doesn't come
with a toy.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.182
It comes with a tiny
bottle of insulin.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.351
There you go, everybody.
That is my monologue joke,

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.852
right there.

00:03:06.852 --> 00:03:08.354
We have a great show tonight.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:11.023
The very funny, the very
talented Jon Hamm is here.

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:13.326
He's gonna talk about this

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:15.094
"Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt"
project

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:17.497
they have comin' up on Netflix.
It's really cool.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:21.333
And he is supporting stjude.org.

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:23.436
Winnie kind of --
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.071
-She was in a rush
to play video games.

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.439
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.641
-"St. Judd."

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.443
St. Jude is the organization.

00:03:31.443 --> 00:03:34.980
Also, Brene Brown,
who is amazing.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.551
She's gonna talk to us
about what's happening right now

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.085
and how we should all
be feeling.

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:43.922
She's just so fun and smart
and charming. I love her.

00:03:43.922 --> 00:03:47.026
And we have great music
from Hailee Steinfeld,

00:03:47.026 --> 00:03:50.429
who's going to do part 1
of her two-part project

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:51.463
that's coming out May 8th.

00:03:51.463 --> 00:03:53.565
It's called
"Half Written Story,"

00:03:53.565 --> 00:03:55.100
is the name of her thing.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:58.004
And we also have
a fun soap opera

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.705
called "The Longest
Days of our Lives"

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:02.041
that I'll get to,
but that's gonna benefit

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.811
The Actors Fund right there.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.746
But [ Laughs ]
you have to see that.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:09.682
Oh, and Salesforce,
I want to say thank you.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:13.219
If you text "meals" to 80100,

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.588
you'll donate $10
to World Central Kitchen

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:20.293
and Salesforce said that they
will match up to $250,000.

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:23.729
So that could be $500,000
going to World Central Kitchen,

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:25.031
which will be amazing.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:27.400
And they're gonna do it
through June 1st.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.668
So we wanna thank our friends
over at Salesforce

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.837
for doing that and working
with us this whole week.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.038
They've been great.

00:04:33.038 --> 00:04:36.275
And for their commitment
to helping families,

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:37.343
small businesses,

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:40.345
and many others affected
by COVID-19.

00:04:40.345 --> 00:04:42.748
Thank you, Salesforce.

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:45.317
I'm feeling
very thankful today,

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.952
to not only them,
but maybe it's a good time

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:48.888
to write out thank-you notes.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:51.190
[ Funk sting plays ]

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.125
-Hi, everybody.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:54.326
-Smile.

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:56.595
[ Laughs ]

00:04:56.595 --> 00:04:58.097
-Hi, Fran.
-Alright. Ready? No, not yet.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:00.466
I don't have music yet.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:01.767
-Oh, good, big yawn.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.436
Friday yawn. Okay.
-Alright.

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.870
Guys, it's Friday.

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:06.806
That's usually when I send out
my thank-you notes.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.440
Can I can get some thank-you
note writing music,

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.508
please, Winnie?

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:12.111
♪♪

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.480
[ Whispering ] Go.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.282
Thank you, "Trolls" movie,

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:19.585
for somehow making
quarantine hair look stylish.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:20.720
Go.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.488
♪♪

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.823
Thank you, tiramisu Oreos,

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:27.627
for being the perfect dessert
after some duck confit

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.661
Hot Pockets.

00:05:29.661 --> 00:05:31.230
[ Laughs ]

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.365
That's it.
That's good.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.800
Thank you, Cinco de May-o --

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.767
Cinco de Mayo,
for being a great day

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:41.340
to enjoy a Mexican beer,
like Modelo, Tecate, or --

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.175
Just Modelo and Tecate.

00:05:43.175 --> 00:05:45.811
Go. next one.

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:46.979
[ Whispering ] Go.

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:48.414
Thank you, squirrels,

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.750
for being the original
panic shoppers.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.951
♪♪

00:05:51.951 --> 00:05:53.652
[ Whispering ] Go.

00:05:53.652 --> 00:05:54.754
Thank you,

00:05:54.754 --> 00:05:56.522
ending of Zoom calls,
-[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:59.925
-for being a mad dash to not be

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:01.861
the last two people
stuck in the room.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.029
Oh, wow.
Hey, Craig.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:05.731
How you doing?
Everything's okay with you?

00:06:05.731 --> 00:06:06.966
Yep.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.634
Thank you, Roombas,

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.903
for looking at us and thinking,
"You're home all day.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.805
Why am I still doing this
for you?" [ Laughs ]

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:17.142
♪♪

00:06:17.142 --> 00:06:18.944
Thank you, ceiling fans,

00:06:18.944 --> 00:06:20.679
for having two speeds --
low

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:22.582
and shaking the entire
house down.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:26.618
♪♪

00:06:26.618 --> 00:06:28.654
Thank you, homeschooling,

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.523
for proving my teachers
were right when they said

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:33.059
I'd need to know how to do
fractions as an adult.

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:35.894
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:35.894 --> 00:06:37.696
-Thank you, butter,

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:39.165
for being the only thing
in the fridge

00:06:39.165 --> 00:06:40.833
with its own studio apartment.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:43.235
♪♪

00:06:43.235 --> 00:06:44.670
[ Whispering ] Go.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.771
No.

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:47.640
♪♪

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.942
Okay, here we go.

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:52.445
Thank you,
"Journey is the destination,"

00:06:52.445 --> 00:06:54.346
for being the motto of people
who have arrived

00:06:54.346 --> 00:06:57.049
at a bad destination.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:59.217
-And finally --

00:06:59.217 --> 00:07:01.820
[ Voices overlapping ]

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.189
Okay, here's the last one.

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:06.158
♪♪

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:08.493
Thank you, Fred and Shaggy
from "Scooby-Doo,"

00:07:08.493 --> 00:07:10.295
for looking like
a before-and-after

00:07:10.295 --> 00:07:11.964
of a guy going
through quarantine.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.533
Guys, that is our show.

00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:16.435
Thank you so much.
What are you doing?

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:18.671
-[ Laughing ]

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:21.140
[ Both humming ]

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.075
-Thank you. Okay.

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:24.410
Stay tuned.
We have a great show.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.777
More "Tonight Show"
when we come back.

00:07:25.777 --> 00:07:28.180
A fun, fun soap opera
with Will Ferrell,

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.383
Kristen Wiig, and a very special
guest -- Jake Gyllenhaal.

